@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Search a large team by name or city
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
actor "Teammate" as actor
box "Frontend — Mondino web app" #E0F2FE
  participant "SearchField" as search
  participant "TeamPage" as page
  participant "filterByStatus / searchRows" as fn
  participant "citySections" as sections
  participant "CitySection" as city
  participant "ListNote" as note
end box
note over page : A team of more than 40: the list has a search\nand one section for each city (L2-056)
actor -> search : Type in "Find a person or city"
search -> page : valueChange(text) on each input event
page -> page : query.set(text); no request, no timer
page -> fn : filterByStatus(rows, filter)
fn --> page : Rows of the chosen filter, west to east
page -> fn : searchRows(rows, query)
fn -> fn : Keep rows whose name or city contains the text,\nwithout regard to case
fn --> page : visibleRows
alt at least one row matches
  page -> sections : citySections(visibleRows, toggled, clock.now(), settings)
  sections -> sections : One section for each city with a match, west to east;\nthe first two open, at most 50 rows in each
  sections --> page : CitySectionContent[]
  page -> city : content, for each section
  city --> actor : The matching teammates, still under their cities (L2-056)
else no row matches
  page -> note : title, text and action
  note --> actor : "No one matches “Reykjavik”", "Try another filter."\nand "Show everyone", in a status region; the text typed shown as text (L2-044)
  actor -> note : Use "Show everyone"
  note -> page : actionChosen
  page -> page : query.set(""); navigate /team (All)
  page --> actor : Every city section again
end
note over page : The filter's counts stay the team's:\n"All 500", "Working now 324", "Asleep 42"
@enduml
